RESULT
  When a downstream host's IGMP Report is transmitted upstream through the IGMP
  Proxy switch, the switch re-originates it so the report appears to come from the
  proxy's UPSTREAM interface - the Source IP is translated.  Verified directly:
      downstream (host-facing)  : group reporter = 10.10.72.20  (the actual host)
      upstream  (router-facing) : group reporter = 10.10.71.2   (u4 upstream SVI)
  The upstream router (u5) never sees the host address; it sees the proxy's
  upstream interface as the reporter.  Multicast data then forwards upstream->
  downstream to the joined host (9/10 sampled).                       => PASS.

  NOTE ON LICENCE/DAEMON: IGMP proxy is the licence-free multicast-forwarding path
  (no PIM).  It needs `ip multicast-routing` and the proxy-service/mroute-proxy
  pair; it does NOT need the AT-IE520-FL01 L3 feature licence.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT / IGMP proxy      : u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0
      upstream interface   : vlan71  10.10.71.2/27   `ip igmp proxy-service`
      downstream interface : vlan72  10.10.72.1/27   `ip igmp mroute-proxy vlan71`
  Upstream router/querier : u5  S/N 264A23066  vlan71 10.10.71.1/27  (IGMP querier)
                            reached over u4<->u5 trunk port1.0.24<->port2.0.24 (vlan71)
  Host / downstream client: tb470 eth2.72  10.10.72.20  (joins the group)
  Host / upstream source  : tb470 eth2.71  10.10.71.20  (sources the data stream)
      both host sub-ifs are tagged on u4 port1.0.2 (trunk vlan71,72).
  Group under test        : 239.10.71.10
  (u2/u3 stack, vlan10 and the u2-facing links are untouched - separate work.)

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA.  The host joins the group on the downstream side with a real scapy
  IGMPv2 report; the proxy's upstream re-origination is proven from the CONTROL
  plane by comparing "Last Reporter" on the downstream (u4) vs the upstream (u5) -
  the definitive evidence of source translation, independent of snooping (which
  forwards the proxied report only toward the querier port, not the host sniffer).
  Data-plane forwarding is then confirmed by sourcing UDP to the group from the
  upstream and counting receipt on the downstream host.  Functional test.

